{ "score": 6, "explanation": "The project demonstrated significant progress in developing drought- and heat-resilient, biofortified bean varieties through completed activities. Specifically, 272 lines were tested across 16 African countries, and 17 Tanzanian varieties were evaluated with 1682 farmers, indicating that the innovation was subjected to semi-controlled testing conditions. This level of testing aligns with Innovation Readiness Level 6, as the innovation was actively tested for its ability to achieve specific impacts under semi-controlled conditions. The involvement of farmers and seed companies in the testing process further supports the readiness level, as it reflects a practical application of the research outcomes. However, the absence of broader uncontrolled testing or proven validation prevents a higher score." }
